It has the letter "m."

258
00:13:28,642 --> 00:13:31,270
We talked about that for an hour.

259
00:13:32,896 --> 00:13:34,147
All right.

260
00:13:35,315 --> 00:13:36,441
Dig in.

261
00:13:37,818 --> 00:13:38,986
Excuse me.

262
00:13:39,278 --> 00:13:40,737
Aren't we going to say grace?

263
00:13:41,071 --> 00:13:43,615
Uh, we don't do that in our house.

264
00:13:44,658 --> 00:13:45,658
0h.

265
00:13:45,701 --> 00:13:47,494
But you're welcome to do so.

266
00:13:47,995 --> 00:13:49,913
That's all right. I don't believe in god.

267
00:13:50,414 --> 00:13:52,165
Well, then why would you say grace?

268
00:13:52,416 --> 00:13:54,501
Because it makes my mom happy.

269
00:13:55,043 --> 00:13:56,503
And why are you wearing mittens?

270
00:13:56,920 --> 00:13:59,172
Well, I don't know where your hands have been.

271
00:14:00,590 --> 00:14:01,590
Okay.

272
00:14:02,384 --> 00:14:03,468
Maybe we should just eat.

273
00:14:09,016 --> 00:14:10,350
Do you like string beans?

274
00:14:12,102 --> 00:14:13,145
No.

275
00:14:14,104 --> 00:14:15,314
But I eat them.

276
00:14:27,701 --> 00:14:29,953
Sheldon, can you hear me?

277
00:14:30,162 --> 00:14:32,706
It's your twin sister, missy.

278
00:14:33,123 --> 00:14:37,044
Everything's all right here, but I think mom misses you real bad.

279
00:14:39,963 --> 00:14:44,634
All right, I can't hear you, so I'm gonna hang up now.

280
00:14:44,926 --> 00:14:46,011
Good night.

281
00:14:49,306 --> 00:14:51,117
I'm telling you, this is a terrible idea.

282
00:14:51,141 --> 00:14:53,741
This is a terrible, terrible idea. He's gonna be fine.

283
00:14:53,935 --> 00:14:55,955
You'll see. I can't believe you're okay with this.

284
00:14:55,979 --> 00:14:57,165
I'm not okay with this.

285
00:14:57,189 --> 00:14:59,107
I'm just trying to be strong for you!

286
00:14:59,316 --> 00:15:02,027
What? You thought him leaving was a good idea.

287
00:15:02,235 --> 00:15:04,555
Oh, I only said that because you thought it was a bad idea.

288
00:15:04,654 --> 00:15:07,199
You know how it's always my nature to go the other way.

289
00:15:07,407 --> 00:15:08,407
Say “up-ll

290
00:15:09,743 --> 00:15:10,743
down.

291
00:15:12,913 --> 00:15:14,039
I'll see you in a bit.

292
00:15:14,331 --> 00:15:15,331
Where are you off to?

293
00:15:15,499 --> 00:15:16,917
I'm going to Dallas to get Sheldon.

294
00:15:17,417 --> 00:15:18,543
Really? Yeah, really.

295
00:15:18,752 --> 00:15:21,088
What about this being a great opportunity for him?

296
00:15:21,713 --> 00:15:22,732
Y'all want me to go or not?

297
00:15:22,756 --> 00:15:24,216
Yes! Go! Yes, and hurry up!

298
00:15:24,424 --> 00:15:25,842
Get a move on, tubby.

299
00:15:26,885 --> 00:15:27,511
Where you going?

300
00:15:27,719 --> 00:15:28,470
To get Sheldon.

301
00:15:28,678 --> 00:15:29,805
Do I get a vote in this?

302
00:15:30,013 --> 00:15:31,014
No.

303
00:15:31,431 --> 00:15:32,431
Dang.

304
00:15:33,225 --> 00:15:39,356
Sleep didn't come easy that night, knowing that, at any moment, I could be decapitated.

305
00:15:40,232 --> 00:15:49,574
And as if that wasn't bad enough, the bed in my room had a dust ruffle, which, to my young mind, only meant one thing: There was dust.

306
00:15:50,158 --> 00:16:00,877
But, eventually, I did drift off, haunted by the memory, the three of us gathered around the piano singing hippie folk music.

307
00:16:01,461 --> 00:16:06,799
J'j'you will not see nothin' like the mighty Quinn j'j' come on. Sing along now.

308
00:16:06,883 --> 00:16:16,435
J'j'come all without j'j' ha! J'j'come all within j'j' j'j'come all within j'j' j'j'you will not see nothin' like the mighty Quinn. J'j'

309
00:16:17,978 --> 00:16:19,855
"You'll not see nothin'."

310
00:16:20,063 --> 00:16:22,107
Shame on whoever wrote that.

311
00:16:39,833 --> 00:16:40,833
Dad?

312
00:16:42,127 --> 00:16:43,127
Yeah?

313
00:16:43,295 --> 00:16:45,213
I'm glad you came to get me.

314
00:16:45,964 --> 00:16:47,090
Me, too.

315
00:16:54,598 --> 00:16:57,433
J'j'...nothing like the mighty Quinn j'j' no!

316
00:16:58,226 --> 00:16:59,478
J'j'come all... if -

317
00:17:11,573 --> 00:17:12,741
You got my message!

318
00:17:14,075 --> 00:17:15,075
Hi-yah!

319
00:17:15,327 --> 00:17:17,621
No hugging! No hugging!

320
00:17:24,836 --> 00:17:27,380
I mean, why'd I bother becoming a teacher?

321
00:17:27,589 --> 00:17:29,382
He knows what I'm gonna say before I say it.

322
00:17:29,591 --> 00:17:31,718
Or I say it and look like a dumbbell. Mm-hmm.

323
00:17:32,052 --> 00:17:34,596
Ms. Ingram, can I offer a suggestion?

324
00:17:34,930 --> 00:17:35,930
What?

325
00:17:36,097 --> 00:17:38,725
Never mind. You do it your way. No, no.

326
00:17:38,934 --> 00:17:41,144
You tell me. Tell me how I'm wrong.

327
00:17:41,353 --> 00:17:45,649
You assumed an extra axiom of euclidean geometry without stating it.

328
00:17:47,108 --> 00:17:48,108
Was he right?

329
00:17:48,235 --> 00:17:49,694
Course he's right.

330
00:17:49,903 --> 00:17:52,322
He's always right.

331
00:17:52,531 --> 00:17:53,865
Tell you what I do.

332
00:17:54,074 --> 00:17:55,242
I send him on little errands.

333
00:17:55,450 --> 00:18:00,247
Like the other day, I told him, "go to the supply room and get me a framastan."

334
00:18:00,664 --> 00:18:01,957
What's a framastan?

335
00:18:02,165 --> 00:18:03,333
No such thing. I made it up.

336
00:18:06,253 --> 00:18:08,797
He was gone the whole period!

337
00:18:09,172 --> 00:18:10,172
That's genius.

338
00:18:10,340 --> 00:18:11,550
I'm using that.

339
00:18:11,758 --> 00:18:13,802
Don't use framastan. That's mine.

340
00:18:16,179 --> 00:18:17,305
What's going on here?

341
00:18:18,098 --> 00:18:20,100
You said he was going away.

342
00:18:20,350 --> 00:18:21,350
Liar.

343
00:18:21,560 --> 00:18:23,019
00 in the morning, guys.
